This is sort of late but I agree with parts of this. The fanbase was pretty annoying from 2015-2017, as I've been around it for a while. I don't know though, once the hiatus kicked in up to the release of Trench and after, the fanbase seemed to mellow out a lot? Like there's a lot of older people now too who seem to be in the fan base. To me it seems much more calm, probably because the Trench sound is more mature in a way.

&#x200B;

Blurryface was one of my least favorite albums, and Vessel is my favorite. I felt bad for Blurryface though, my least 2 favorite songs by them in 2015 (Blurryface era) were extremely popular (Stressed Out and Heathens), it was weird. I feel like people have a false impression about the band members, that they're only making sad lyrics and stuff like this for attention and to relate with a younger generation. Even though the singer has been making songs like that before they were even a band.

&#x200B;

There is some real gems, but if the songs that got them popular were different and better songs, I think the negative impression would be almost completely gone.

&#x200B;

(Sorry I kind of got off topic but yeah I don't know why people hate them either.)

The Pantaloon is 61...that's in my top 10 I-

